  "method": "Aperture photometry at a fixed position on the native SPHEREx pixels (IMAGE - ZODI, MJy/sr) of each epoch's exposure: a circular aperture of radius aperture_arcsec with exact pixel overlap, minus the median of a sky annulus from aperture + 12\" to aperture + 36\"; flux_err from the VARIANCE plane plus the sky-median error. No aperture correction, so point-source fluxes are low. Any masked, saturated or off-frame pixel in the aperture gives a null flux and quality bad.",
